# Split from server.lang - dialogue bundle (aetherhaven_dialogue_chef)
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_abandoned.body=Suit yourself. I'll keep judging Corin's stew from a safe distance until you change your mind.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_abandoned.c0=Fair enough.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_abandoned.speaker=Pepper Ashford
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_accepted.body=Good. I'll be at the inn until there's a kitchen worth walking into. Stake the plot, get the walls up, then come drag me over when it smells like food instead of damp wood.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_accepted.c0=I'll get it built.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_accepted.speaker=Pepper Ashford
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_building.body=Still waiting on an actual kitchen. Tables help too. Come back when I can cook without balancing a pan on hopes and prayers.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_building.c0=I need to drop the quest.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_building.c1=Still working on it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_building.speaker=Pepper Ashford
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_done.body=Finally. Heat where it belongs, counters that don't lean, chairs that look like people might sit in them. About time this place ate properly.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_done.c0=Let's keep talking.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_done.speaker=Pepper Ashford
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_quest_restaurant.body=Look, Corin keeps people warm and fed, and I respect that. What I don't respect is calling a shared kettle cooking. Get me a real kitchen. Counter, stove, seats. I'll put a token in your hand. Stake it, build it, then come find me when the place isn't imaginary.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_quest_restaurant.c0=We'll build it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_quest_restaurant.c1=Not right now.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.pepper_quest_restaurant.speaker=Pepper Ashford
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.rep_reward_50.speaker=Pepper Ashford
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.root.body=I'm Pepper. I cook. Properly. Corin's hearth is fine if you only care about surviving the night, but if you want food that makes people linger, you came to the right temperamental cook.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.root.c5=How's the restaurant treating you?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.root.c6=The restaurant is ready for you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.root.c7=About the restaurant...
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.root.c8=You look like you want a kitchen of your own.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.root.c9=Catch you later.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.root.speaker=Pepper Ashford
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.gift.love=Oh. That one I actually want. Thank you. You may sit wherever you like tonight.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.gift.like=Not bad. I can work with this.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.gift.neutral=I'll find a shelf for it. Eventually.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.gift.dislike=If this is a joke, it needs more seasoning. Keep it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.fallback=Well? Talk, or make room for someone who will.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.0=Careful. Hot pans and hot tempers. Ask what you need before I decide the onions are more interesting.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.1=If that bag is raw meat with no plan, walk it back outside. I'm not a campfire with opinions.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.2=I have about two free minutes between orders. Use them wisely.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.3=Corin offered me stew again. I smiled. I declined. We're still friends somehow.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.4=Hungry? Sit. Fidgeting over the counter only makes the food late.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.5=Sharpened the knives this morning. Don't make me demonstrate.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.6=Most people come for a plate. A few come to chat. I allow both if they stay out of my way.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.7=You can taste when someone actually cares about the pan. That's the whole job.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.8=I just wiped that counter. Hands to yourself unless you're paying.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.greeting.9=If it smells like onions, relax. If it smells like something dying, shout.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.hint.love.0=Recipes, cookware, anything that belongs near a stove. Those land soft with me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.hint.love.1=Bring me something worth cooking and I might forget to scowl for a second.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.hint.love.2=A good ingredient does more for me than a long speech.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.hint.dislike.0=Raw scraps and trash do not enter this kitchen. Full stop.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.hint.dislike.1=Rocks and refuse are not clever gifts. They're chores.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_chef.main_hub.hint.dislike.2=If it smells like the bin, leave it in your pack where I can't see it.
